<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Togha Temür</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1353</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Togha Temür was a Mongol prince descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Chinggis Khan</a>'s brother Jochi Qasar who claimed the throne of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> after the death of Abu Sa'id in 1335. Based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorgan">Gurgan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a>, he controlled much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a> and was recognised as overlord for a time by the Sarbadars. The Sarbadars defeated him and in 1353 had him murdered, ending the last Ilkhanid claim in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/togha-temur.jpg" alt="Togha Temür" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: American Numismatic Society · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_Dinar_of_Taghaytimur,_Kashan,_739_H,_1338-1339.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
